# Mainnet Environment Configuration (PRODUCTION)
#
# ⚠️  SECURITY CRITICAL - This file contains secrets for real money
#
# Copy to .env.mainnet (DO NOT COMMIT TO GIT):
#   cp .env.mainnet.example .env.mainnet
#   # Edit with your actual password
#
# Use with:
#   docker compose --env-file .env.mainnet -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml up -d
#
# Verification:
#   - .env.mainnet should be in .gitignore
#   - Never paste this file into logs, bug reports, or public channels
#   - Store backups securely (1Password, LastPass, AWS Secrets Manager, etc)
#

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED: ZECD RPC PASSWORD
# ============================================================================

# Generate a strong random password:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# This MUST match the [rpc] password in deploy/zecd.btc-mainnet.toml
# CHANGE THIS VALUE BEFORE DEPLOYING
ZECD_RPC_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME_TO_A_STRONG_PASSWORD_USE_openssl_rand_base64_32

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: BITCOIN DATA DIRECTORY
# ============================================================================

# Only needed if your bitcoind datadir is not at /mnt/data/bitcoin_data
# Path must already be synced with the mainnet blockchain
# BITCOIN_DATADIR=/mnt/data/bitcoin_data

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL: ADVANCED SETTINGS
# ============================================================================

# UI server port inside the container (almost always 8080)
# External port binding is loopback-only by default (127.0.0.1:8080)
# UI_PORT=8080

# If using full mode (JSON-RPC bitcoind instead of kyoto):
# Bitcoind RPC endpoint (localhost only, no internet exposure)
# BITCOIND_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8332

# ============================================================================
# PRODUCTION CHECKLIST
# ============================================================================
#
# Before deploying to production:
#
# [ ] Generate a strong random password:
#     openssl rand -base64 32
#
# [ ] Update ZECD_RPC_PASSWORD above with that password
#
# [ ] Verify .env.mainnet is in .gitignore:
#     grep "\.env\.mainnet" ../.gitignore
#
# [ ] Keep a backup in a secure location (1Password, LastPass, etc)
#     NOT in this repo or any unencrypted backup
#
# [ ] Ensure bitcoind is synced before starting zecd:
#     docker compose -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml exec bitcoind \
#         bitcoin-cli getblockchaininfo | grep initialblockdownload
#     (should show: "initialblockdownload": false)
#
# [ ] Start the stack with the .env file:
#     docker compose --env-file .env.mainnet -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml up -d
#
# [ ] Verify the UI is running and healthy:
#     docker compose -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml ps
#     docker compose -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml logs zecd-btc-ui
#
# [ ] Access the UI only via loopback (not internet-facing):
#     curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/info
#
# [ ] For internet access, use a reverse proxy with TLS:
#     - nginx with Let's Encrypt SSL
#     - traefik with automatic cert renewal
#     - caddy with automatic HTTPS
#
# ============================================================================
# PASSWORD ROTATION
# ============================================================================
#
# To rotate the RPC password:
#
# 1. Generate a new password:
#    NEW_PASS=$(openssl rand -base64 32)
#    echo $NEW_PASS
#
# 2. Update deploy/zecd.btc-mainnet.toml:
#    [rpc]
#    password = "NEW_PASS"
#
# 3. Update this .env.mainnet file:
#    ZECD_RPC_PASSWORD=NEW_PASS
#
# 4. Restart the containers:
#    docker compose --env-file .env.mainnet -f docker-compose.btc-mainnet.yml restart
#
# ============================================================================
# EMERGENCY PROCEDURES
# ============================================================================
#
# If you accidentally commit .env.mainnet to git:
#
# 1. IMMEDIATELY rotate the password (see above)
#
# 2. Remove the file from git history:
#    git rm --cached deploy/.env.mainnet
#    git commit -m "Remove .env.mainnet (password compromised, rotated)"
#    git push
#
# 3. Verify it's not in the commit:
#    git log -p deploy/.env.mainnet  # should be empty
#
# 4. Check git history for secrets:
#    git log -p | grep "ZECD_RPC_PASSWORD\|rpc_password"
#
# ============================================================================
